==In the manga==
[[File:Musician Adventures.png|140px|thumb|A Musician in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
====={{MangaArc|Black & White}}=====
A Musician appeared with his {{p|Eelektrik}} in ''[[PS486|Unraveling Mysteries]]''. He is based on Musician Preston who appears in [[Unova Route 5]] in {{game|Black and White|s}} and {{B2W2}}.

Another Musician appeared in ''[[PS500|With a Little Help From My Friends]]''. He was based on the Musician who plays the guitar in Café Sonata and teaches {{p|Meloetta}} {{m|Relic Song}} in the {{pkmn|games}}. He was impressed by {{adv|Bianca}}'s flute performances that White recorded and sent to him, and invited the two to Café Sonata. By the time White and Bianca arrived, he was being attacked by a wild {{p|Vullaby}}, and his hand was broken as a result of the attack, which left him unable to play the guitar.

===={{MangaArc|Sword & Shield}}====
A Musician was briefly shown at [[Hammerlocke]] in ''[[PASS17|Stealth!! Infiltrate the Energy Plant]]''.

In ''[[PASS18|Chomp!! It's Dracovish]]'', a Musician named '''Eric''' (Japanese: '''トシユキ''' ''Toshiyuki'') from {{tc|Macro Cosmos's}} in disguise was sent with his cohorts to [[Route 9 Tunnel]] to dispose of a wild {{p|Dracovish}} that suddenly [[Dynamax]]ed. The Dracovish was saved by [[Marvin]], who used his [[Sniffler]] to stun everyone long enough for him to catch Dracovish and escape. Afterward, Eric and the others reported their failure to [[Oleana]] and were ordered to stand by in [[Wyndon]].

===={{MangaArc|Scarlet & Violet}}==== 
[[File:Mireia Adventures.png|140px|thumb|Mireia in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
In ''[[PASV10|Evolve! The Second Fire Evolution!!]]'', {{Violet}} and {{adv|Arven}} met Mireia (Japanese: '''ケイコ''' ''Keiko''), a street performer that plays music on [[West Province (Area One)]]. One day, {{p|Bombirdier}}, the Open Sky {{pkmn2|Titan}}, appeared, causing Mireia's listeners to dwindle in number. Mireia tried calming the rampaging Titan with her music, only to anger it and get injured in the process.

In ''[[PASV11|Decisive! The Battle in the Sky!!]]'', Mireia helped Violet and Arven battle the Titan by luring it away with her music, giving the others the opportunity to take it down. As thanks for her assistance, Violet and Arven offered to buy one of Mireia's CDs, but she refused. Mireia explained that she wanted people to buy her music because they genuinely liked it, not because they owed her a favor. Arven instead repaid his debt by treating Mireia to a [[sandwich]] made from the [[Bitter Herba Mystica]] the Titan Bombirdier was guarding.
